+# Firmware sources
+
+## Regulatory database
+
+`regulatory.db` and `regulatory.db.p7s` are built from:
+
+- wireless-regdb 2026.05.30
+- https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/sforshee/wireless-regdb.git
+
+They are embedded into the kernel via `CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE`.
+OpenWrt's `wireless-regdb` package is disabled to avoid a second copy.
+
+## MT76 WiFi firmware
+
+The MediaTek mt76 firmware binaries are from:
+
+- linux-firmware
+- https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/firmware/linux-firmware.git/tree/mediatek
+
+They are proprietary MediaTek firmware; redistribution follows
+linux-firmware's `LICENCE.mediatek`.
+
+Bundled files:
+
+- mt7610e.bin
+- mt7610u.bin
+- mt7662.bin
+- mt7662_rom_patch.bin
+- mt7662u.bin
+- mt7662u_rom_patch.bin
+- mt7663_n9_rebb.bin
+- mt7663_n9_v3.bin
+- mt7663pr2h.bin
+- mt7663pr2h_rebb.bin
+- WIFI_MT7961_patch_mcu_1_2_hdr.bin
+- WIFI_MT7961_patch_mcu_1a_2_hdr.bin
+- WIFI_RAM_CODE_MT7961_1.bin
+- WIFI_RAM_CODE_MT7961_1a.bin
+- mt7925/WIFI_MT7925_PATCH_MCU_1_1_hdr.bin
+- mt7925/WIFI_RAM_CODE_MT7925_1_1.bin
+
+These files are embedded into the kernel via `CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE`.
+The OpenWrt mt76 firmware package is not used.
+
+## MT76 driver source
+
+The mt76 WiFi drivers use the Linux 7.3 kernel tree's own source at
+`drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/`, built directly into the kernel
+image. OpenWrt's external mt76 tree is no longer overlaid.
+
+
+The kernel keeps built-in `cfg80211`, `mac80211` and `rfkill`; mt76 is
+built into the kernel image as built-in drivers. The kernel's `CONFIG_MT76*`
+and `CONFIG_MT79*` options are set to `=y`.
+
+The firmware files listed above are embedded into the kernel through
+`CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE`; the rootfs does not include
+`/lib/firmware/mediatek` and does not install `kmod-mt7921-firmware` or
+`kmod-mt7925-firmware`.
